  "note": "H0 of SPA: no strategy beats cash (zero excess return); StepM lists strategies that do at FWER 5%; PBO = share of CSCV splits whose in-sample best is at or below the out-of-sample median. The full trial family contains configurations that price ATM options at the VIX (\u03b2 = 1: bridge rows 0-10 and the \u03b2 = 1.00 grid row); a rejection or a low PBO there that comes from those rows measures the mis-specified mark, not a strategy \u2014 compare the beta_estimated subset. A low PBO says the in-sample ranking persists out of sample; it is not evidence of skill: the configurations differ mostly by persistent level effects (the \u03b2 of the mark, a sleeve's net short- or long-vol exposure) that move every sub-period alike and keep ranks stable with or without skill. Read it with oos_sharpe_of_selected_mean and oos_on_is_slope (< 0: the in-sample winners' out-of-sample Sharpe falls as their in-sample Sharpe rises)",
